1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:11,500
Avizis — Transparent Agent Computation Graph
A live debugger for AI agents: watch, steer, replay.

2
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:31,000
The agent turns a task into a computation graph
and executes it step by step.

3
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:40,500
A decision fork: the agent asks the user
to choose a direction.

4
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:51,500
The chosen branch activates —
the rest of the fork fades out.

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The supervisor adds new steps dynamically
as work progresses (graph v2… v10).

6
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:14,500
A second fork — content delivery method.

7
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:26,500
Hands-on simulation chosen — the graph adapts.

8
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:35,500
Run 1 completed: 19 nodes, 29 LLM calls,
full token and cost audit.

9
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:47,500
Node inspector: input, output, reason for adding
— every step stays transparent.

10
00:01:48,500 --> 00:02:07,500
Timeline scrubbing: replay any moment
of the run, frame by frame.

11
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:21,500
Run 2: a support-triage agent —
this time decisions are in auto mode.

12
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:35,500
The plan grows as the supervisor
keeps analyzing the results.

13
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:49,500
A node fails (API rate limit) —
the run stops. Nothing is hidden.

14
00:02:50,500 --> 00:03:03,500
The user retries the failed node
right from the inspector.

15
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:21,000
The retried node succeeds —
and the fork is resolved by the agent itself.

16
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:35,500
The supervisor keeps extending the plan
(v8… v12).

17
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:53,500
Run 2 completed — after a human
intervention in the middle of the run.

18
00:03:54,500 --> 00:04:05,500
Every run stays in history: replay, inspect,
export an audit report (Markdown).

19
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
github.com/danku13/Avizis
